    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an administrative operations assistant.\n\nAnalyze the incoming administrative request and classify it for proper routing and follow-up.\n\nRequester: {{ $json.requester_name }}\nEmail: {{ $json.requester_email }}\nDepartment: {{ $json.department }}\nSubject: {{ $json.subject }}\nRequest Details: {{ $json.request_details }}\nRequested Deadline: {{ $json.requested_deadline }}\n\nReturn the following information:\n\n* category\n* priority\n* summary\n* action_required\n* suggested_deadline\n* requires_notification\n\nCategory must be one of:\n\n* Document Request\n* Scheduling\n* Finance/Admin\n* Procurement\n* Customer/Client Concern\n* Internal Support\n* General Inquiry\n* Other\n\nPriority must be one of:\n\n* Low\n* Medium\n* High\n* Urgent\n\nPriority definitions:\n\n* Low = Routine request with no meaningful time pressure.\n* Medium = Standard request that should be handled through the normal administrative workflow.\n* High = Important and time-sensitive, but does not require immediate action within hours.\n* Urgent = Immediate action is required, usually within hours or the same day. Failure to act could cause a missed critical deadline, compliance issue, financial impact, operational disruption, or blocked business process.\n\nrequires_notification must be true for High or Urgent requests, otherwise false.\n\nKeep the summary concise and business-like.\n\nDo not classify a request as Urgent only because the requester uses words such as \"urgent\" or \"ASAP\". Base the priority on the actual deadline, business impact, and consequences described in the request.",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        352,
        0
      ],
